## Coding Summary (v4)

- **Dominant codes:** `D1.3 > Anti_Socialism_Anti_Collectivism` (x2), `D1.1 > Anti_Casta`, `D1.1 > Delegitimization_of_Regulation`, `D1.2 > Attack_on_Experts_and_Technocrats`.
- **Sub-dimension balance:** D1.1 (2), D1.2 (1), D1.3 (2). One of the most ideologically dense and rhetorically extreme speeches in this stretch of the corpus — bookended by two escalating anti-socialism passages ("en el límite asesina" and "enfermedad del alma") that develop the theme from consequentialist harm to psychological/moral pathology.
- **New inductive categories added:** none.
- **Notable rhetorical moves:** The "en el límite asesina" opening passage is notable for using near-murder-accusation language against socialism/"justicia social" generally, in a register similar to (though not identical to) the "asesinos verdes" passage at the Tech Forum speech three weeks earlier — worth tracking as part of an emerging pattern of increasingly extreme moral-condemnation language in late-2024 speeches. The "enfermedad del alma" passage is a distinctive psychopathologizing move, framing socialist belief itself (not just its policy consequences) as a character/spiritual defect.
- **Overcoding decisions:** The Reagan quote and Huerta de Soto citation were treated as elaboration of the same opening Anti_Socialism_Anti_Collectivism instance rather than separate codes, since they reinforce rather than introduce a new rhetorical move. The extensive fiscal/disinflation achievement recap was left uncoded as repetition of content coded extensively elsewhere in this batch.
- **V3 recoding notes:** N/A — first-pass v4 coding.
- **Flagged for follow-up:** No direct climate content, but the "en el límite asesina" and "enfermedad del alma" passages should be cross-referenced with the Tech Forum "asesinos verdes" passage (2024-10-19) when the paper discusses the escalating moral register of Milei's ideological-adversary rhetoric in late 2024, even though this particular speech's target is socialism generally rather than environmentalism specifically.
